every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the rook on a7.","The next best move, 20.Nb2, would drop White's winning chances from 49% to 32% (−2.09).","20.Rxa7 stops …Rxc7.","Black was threatening …Rxc7, winning a bishop. Rxa7 takes care of it.","Trades rooks.","The rook on a7 can be taken by the bishop on c5."]},{"ply":73,"name":"37.Kg2","cls":"mistake","color":"w","headline":"37.Kg2 is a mistake: White's winning chances go from 46% to 29%.","points":["Black answers 37…Rc3: the rook takes the open c-file.","Better was 37.Rh4 (−0.45)."],"better":"37.Rh4 stops …Qxf3. After 37…Kf8 38.Rf4 Qc1+ 39.Kg2 Qb2 40.Qxh6+ Ke7, White comes out a pawn up (−0.45)."},{"ply":74,"name":"37…e5","cls":"miss","color":"b","headline":"37…e5 misses the chance 37.Kg2 gave: 37…Rc3 would have punished it. Black's winning chances go from 71% to 54%.","points":["White answers 38.Qg4+, which brings the queen, White's least active piece, into play (from 6 to 9 usable squares).","Better was 37…Rc3 (−2.43): the rook takes the open c-file."],"better":"37…Rc3 stops Rh4 and takes the open c-file. Engine line: 38.Rf4 e5 39.Rf5 Rc2 40.Kh3 Qe6 (−2.43)."},{"ply":85,"name":"43.Rxa6","cls":"mistake","color":"w","headline":"43.Rxa6 is a mistake: White's winning chances go from 45% to 32%.","points":["Black answers 43…e4, which attacks the knight on f3.","Better was 43.Rc8 (−0.58): the rook takes the open c-file."],"better":"43.Rc8 threatens Rxc5, winning a bishop. Engine line: 43…Rd5 44.Nh4 e4 45.Kf1 f5 46.Rc6 (−0.58)."},{"ply":86,"name":"43…e4","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"43…e4! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Attacks the knight on f3.","Gains space: the pawn on e4 cramps White's pieces behind it.","The next best move, 43…Rc3, would drop Black's winning chances from 68% to 51% (−0.09).","43…e4 attacks the knight on f3.","White answers 44.Ng1.","After 44.Ng1 Rd2 45.Nh3 e3 46.Ra4 Bd4 47.Rxd4 Rxd4 48.fxe3 Ra4, Black comes out a pawn up (−1.16)."]},{"ply":88,"name":"44…Rd2","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"44…Rd2! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The rook reaches the seventh rank, where 3 pawns sit.","Adds a decisive attacker on the f2 pawn: 2 attackers against 1 defender.","The next best move, 44…Rd1, would drop Black's winning chances from 69% to 50% (−0.02).","44…Rd2 wins a pawn, picking it up with 45…Rxf2+.","Sets up a sequence and wins a pawn once the captures settle, picking it up with 45…Rxf2+.","White answers 45.Ra5, attacking the bishop on c5, which is undefended."]},{"ply":93,"name":"47.Ra4","cls":"blunder","color":"w","headline":"47.Ra4 is a blunder: White's winning chances go from 50% to 10%.","points":["Black answers 47…Bg1: the bishop aims at the h2 pawn, a weak point in front of the White king.","Better was 47.Rxf6 (−0.03), which takes the pawn on f6."],"better":"47.Rxf6 takes the f6 pawn and attacks the f7 pawn, which is undefended. After 47…Kg8 48.Rd6 Rxa2 49.Nh6+ Kh7 50.Nxf7 Bg1, White comes out a pawn up (−0.03)."},{"ply":94,"name":"47…Bg1","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"47…Bg1! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The bishop aims at the h2 pawn, a weak point in front of the White king.","Moving away uncovers the rook on d2, which now hits the h2 pawn.","The next best move, 47…e3, would drop Black's winning chances from 90% to 69% (−2.23).","47…Bg1 threatens …Rxh2#, with mate in 1, and wins a knight for two pawns, picking it up with 49…Bxe3.","It threatens …Rxh2#, with mate in 1, so White has to spend the next move on it.","Sets up a sequence and wins a knight for two pawns once the captures settle, picking it up with 49…Bxe3."]}],"opening":{"name":"Rapport-Jobava System","eco":"D01","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 5…a6: 10 moves in all, 5 by White and 5 by Black.","Theory runs out after 5…a6: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}